The root cause is the behavior of `this`. Within a standard `function`, `this` does not reference the `Timer` object. Since `setInterval` independently invokes the function, `this` resolves to either the global object (or `undefined` if strict mode is enabled). Consequently, `this.seconds` becomes `undefined`, and performing arithmetic on `undefined` (adding 1) produces `NaN`.

